Fix intermittent failures of the upstream service (SRV) tests.

Angie resolves "resolve" stream/http upstreams eagerly at worker startup,
caching the DNS stub's default answer for the configured "valid" time.
The tests update the stub and then wait for the resolver to re-resolve,
but a single re-resolution cycle may still be processed by angie after the
very next test connection is made, so the connection can use the previous
set of upstream addresses (e.g. "127.0.0.1:PORT" instead of
"127.0.0.201:PORT").  This shows up as flaky failures of tests like
'log - A' / 'log - A full' in stream_upstream_service.t.

Wait for two full re-resolution cycles (instead of one) after an update so
that angie had enough time to apply the new addresses to the upstream peer
list before the test proceeds with connections.

--- a/tests/stream_upstream_service.t
+++ b/tests/stream_upstream_service.t
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@
 
 		# let resolver cache expire to finish upstream reconfiguration
 		select undef, undef, undef, 0.5;
-		last unless ($gen + $plan > $gen2);
+		last unless ($gen + 2 * $plan > $gen2);
 	}
 }
 
--- a/tests/upstream_service.t
+++ b/tests/upstream_service.t
@@ -280,7 +280,7 @@
 
 		# let resolver cache expire to finish upstream reconfiguration
 		select undef, undef, undef, 0.5;
-		last unless ($gen + $plan > $gen2);
+		last unless ($gen + 2 * $plan > $gen2);
 	}
 }